From ca7f590ab1a622a2a675913d10cb93f33d68a5b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 22:10:28 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] net: ethernet: broadcom: add Kona ESUB Ethernet driver

The BCM281xx (Capri) ESUB is a ROBO-style switch (ESW) with two RGMII
ports and an internal management port (IMP) wired to the CPU through
two FIFOs: MTP (memory to port, transmit) and PTM (port to memory,
receive), each fed by a channel of the ESUB DesignWare AHB DMA.

Register layout, DMA descriptor format, the 4-byte Broadcom tag and the
PTM/MTP setup follow Broadcom's u-boot bcm11140_eth driver and the
island_net.c driver in Roku's linux-3.0.82 GPL release. Notable details:
- the PTM config register is ESW+0x80008; writing ESW+0x80000 instead
  makes received data arrive byte-reversed within each 64-bit word
- the DMA does not check descriptor ownership, so after an RX overrun
  the ring is re-synced to the oldest filled slot (as island_net does)
- switch registers need 64-bit accesses and a dummy chipreg read first

RX is NAPI polled from an hrtimer (no IRQ yet), TX is synchronous.

Co-Authored-By: Vas <banoz@users.noreply.github.com>
